$WW,1$$FG,14$$TX+CX,"Codex of Nous"$$FG$

$TX+CX,"A browser for the lore of the temple"$

The left pane lists entries.  The right pane shows the selected entry,
word-wrapped to the window.

$FG,10$Controls$FG$
  $FG,11$Up / Down$FG$   - Select an entry
  $FG,11$PgUp / PgDn$FG$ - Scroll the entry
  $FG,11$Home / End$FG$  - Jump to the top or bottom
  $FG,11$Tab$FG$         - Select the next entry
  $FG,11$Enter$FG$       - Reload the lore directory
  $FG,11$Esc$FG$         - Quit

$FG,10$Lore sources$FG$
If $FG,11$::/Hermes/Lore$FG$ exists, Codex reads every $FG,11$*.DD$FG$
and $FG,11$*.TXT$FG$ beneath it and shows the plain text.  When that
directory is absent it opens a short bundled sample instead.

$FG,10$Art$FG$
The header uses $FG,11$Hermes/Art/Icons/32/codex-of-nous$FG$ in the
standard sixteen-color temple palette.
